"""Pin the MTSO suites that MToP also ships to its reference.

Values from MToP (D:/MatlabPlatform/MTO-Platform-master) in MATLAB R2020b,
through each problem's own task handles, stored so the agreement keeps being
checked without MATLAB. Covers the first three tasks of each problem, which is
enough to pin the shift and rotation data every task draws from.

Two suites are not covered here because MToP has no counterpart: CEC17MTSO_10D
and ManyTask_10D are defined by DDMTOLab itself.

STOP's Quartic tasks add a U[0,1) term by design, on both platforms, so they
are compared on their deterministic part.
"""
